there are several cool and weird  discoveries and stories to come across  in assassin's creed valhalla  some are structured as multi-part quests  while others are just  random findings that you want to go  looking for there are way too many to  list but we've compiled a few of our  favorites we'll try to avoid spoilers as  best we can  but we do have to mention the names of  certain characters and places just to  let you know where to go  in order to find whatever we're talking  about  over the course of the game more people  want to come and join avor settlement in  england one of them being  vulka from your home back in norway  you'll need a level 3 settlement to  convince her to come and join you  but when she does make sure to build her  hut as soon as you can and follow her  quest line  she'll brew you a potion and you'll be  transported to asgard  yep you heard me and actually asgard is  a huge part of the game and surprisingly  easy to miss so consider this your psa  as per tradition a great deal of  valhalla is someone in the present day  using an animus to relive the memories  of someone in the past  unlike the older games in the series  however valhalla doesn't pull you out of  the animus all that often  but that doesn't mean you shouldn't just  hop out every once in a while  i went through hell to bring you here  it'd better be worth it  there's actually a gold mine of lore to  pick through in the modern day  especially on layla's laptop  it's in old files emails and audio  recordings that you'll see additional  context  for valhalla's overall theme that of  fate  leila can talk to her allies as well and  the two will usually have new things to  talk about after significant  developments  in avor story the game won't tell you  about this though if you want to hear  those conversations you'll need to  choose to leave the animus on your own  also make sure to root through layla's  emails you'll find a nod to a certain  global pandemic in there  though avor only teams up with the  hidden ones in order to root the order  of ancients out of england and make the  country safer for their clan they can  take a few more additional steps towards  joining the group  like donning the robes of england's  hidden ones there are actually two  different assassin based armor sets in  the game  the first the hidden one armor increases  your assassination and headshot damage  each armor piece is located in one of  the hidden one bureaus scattered across  england to find them you'll have to  think like a member of the brotherhood  and take into account the history of  england look for the centers of power  back when rome still ruled  england if you're having trouble you can  find a few clues to the bureau's  locations as layla in the modern day  the second the mentor armor allows you  to dress as the leader of the hidden  ones increasing attack power and overall  speed  there is no deductive reasoning for  figuring out where the pieces of the  mentor armor are hidden  but you don't have to guess entirely  like other armor sets finding at least  one  piece and looking at the description of  that piece will tell you where the  others are  if you travel to the forest in the  northeastern part of grant bridgeshire  at night you may be able to spot  fireflies these bright little bugs are  both hard to find  and very fast but if you manage to catch  them you can bring them to the pond  behind your settlement's longhouse  they'll set your settlement to glow come  night time  deep in the lands of east anglia is a  small ransacked home  an almost mystical aura hangs in the air  and scattered notes tell a frightening  story of a man and his three daughters  it is not a welcoming place but those  willing to press on will find a nearby  tomb  hiding a piece of gear behind a locked  door and the door needs  three keys statue has three large slits  something may fit here a knife or a  dagger  if you're having trouble finding this  place go to the easternmost area of the  kingdom  to actually unlock the door and enter  the crypt you'll need to hunt down the  three daughters best each one in combat  and claim their daggers just be careful  each can command a different element and  they hit  pretty hard they aren't bosses you want  to go up against in the early game  unless you've unlocked some powerful  combat abilities  upon finding stonehenge make sure to  explore the nearby area until you find a  cave go inside it and you'll find a very  cool weapon  excalibur that's right king arthur's  legendary blade is there for you to  claim  an ancient weapon  except it's not as simple as that you  need 11 keys to unlock it some keys are  found by completing platforming  challenges inside caves scattered around  england and others are held by zealots  who serve the order of ancients  if you have no idea what you're  searching for you'll actually have to go  into one of the caves for valka's quest  so that will give you an idea what to  look out for zealots are a bit  easier to find they'll traditionally  stick to main roads so just travel along  the main roads and you'll run into them  eventually  in wessex there's a snake carved into  the hillside no  quest here as far as we can tell but  quite a few snakes spawn here  and there's a treasure located here  though you'll first have to discover a  map that tells you which part of the  snake is hiding the prize you seek  until then the place is just a really  good spot to go in order to hunt snakes  those roman artifacts that you may have  discovered in your journey across  england they can be used to outfit a  museum for your settlement expand the  settlement a few times and it will  attract a rather rambunctious fellow  who's  very enthusiastic about rome evil  have you ever been in love build him a  museum and it will kick off a hunt for  these artifacts as well as a pretty  funny  side story that involves the rivalry  between two collectors  a giant wall protects the northern  border of england from the rest of the  world you can travel along the full  length of it lighting the signal fires  as you go you get an achievement  trophy for lighting all of them plus you  meet a fairly interesting and violent  chap on the wall who will challenge you  to a fight  not a quest there's no reason to travel  the length of the wall and light these  signal fires but it will see you explore  the most northern part of the map which  is a beautiful sight to behold  so there you have it some cool things  from ac valhalla that you might have  missed what were your favorites let us  know in the comments below and for more  on valhalla  including graphics comparisons beginners  tips a review and more  keep it a game spot  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

